\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  I'm not ashamed to own my Lord,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Or to defend His cause,
\par  Maintain the glory of His Cross,
\par And honour all His laws.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  Jesus, my Lord! I know His Name,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  His name is all my boast;
\par  Nor will He put my soul to shame,
\par  Nor let my hope be lost.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. I know that safe with Him remains,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Protected by His power,
\par What I've committed to His trust,
\par Till the decisive hour.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then will He own His servant's name
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  Before His Father's face,
\par And in the New Jerusalem
\par \pard     Appoint my soul a place.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

